WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Picture a hall with a throne.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.330
No king or queen ever sits on it.

3
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.250
Behind it, a kitchen.

4
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.320
Volunteers cook, serve and wash
up, and every meal is free.

5
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.870
Outside, a tall flagpole wrapped in cloth.

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.040
Its flag is renewed
every year at Vaisakhi.

7
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.030
This is a gurdwara.

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.700
So why does a Sikh place
of worship need all three?

9
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.380
In this mission, you'll
walk through a gurdwara,

10
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.060
from the flag outside to the prayer hall.

11
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:34.830
Then you'll explore what happens there,
and how much it matters to Sikhs today.

12
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.450
Your mission: find out why
a gurdwara has a kitchen,

13
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.870
a throne and a flag you
can see from far away.
